# DTF tier manifest: popularity-homoglyph-affix  (#2956 / follow-up to #2952/#2949 / 1.7.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. Extends the typed `popularity` curation
# rule's typo-squat arm with two evasion classes pure Damerau-Levenshtein
# (max_distance<=2) misses:
#   - Unicode-confusable (homoglyph) impersonation: >=3 confusable codepoint
#     swaps (Cyrillic е U+0435 / ѕ U+0455 for Latin e/s) exceed max_distance
#     while staying pixel-identical. #2956 folds names through NFKC + the
#     UTS #39 confusable skeleton (unicode-security crate) and flags a
#     skeleton collision with a popular name whose raw name differs, plus
#     mixed-script identifiers as a standalone signal.
#   - Affix reputation-riding: a popular base name wrapped in ANY boundary-
#     delimited affix token ('python-requests', 'data-numpy', 'numpy2024',
#     camelCase), matched in skeleton space, is len(affix)+1 edits away.
#     #2956 flags it only while the CANDIDATE itself is low/unknown-download
#     (affix_max_downloads gate) and not itself on the popular list — the
#     false-positive guard for legitimately popular affixed names
#     ('python-dateutil').
#   - Mixed-script is proximity-gated: a multi-script name only flags when it
#     also sits near a popular name in skeleton space; benign
#     internationalized names must not flood review.
#
# Enforcement seam (unchanged from curation-global-popularity): the STAGING-
# CATALOG re-evaluate layer (POST /curation/packages/re-evaluate ->
# curation_packages.status/.rule_id/.evaluation_reason). Advisory Flag ->
# review by default; no new enforcement path.
#
# NO-EGRESS SCOPE: every download count degrades to Unknown, so EVERY pypi
# package lands in `review` with "popularity unknown" on both baseline and
# fix. Status alone is therefore NOT discriminating — the oracle asserts on
# the evaluation_reason CONTENT:
#   (RULE)      global popularity rule (typosquat_check on, max_distance 2,
#               defaults for homoglyph/affix) -> 201 + rule_type echoed.
#   (HOMOGLYPH) 'rеquеѕts' (3 Cyrillic swaps of 'requests', D-L distance 3 >
#               max_distance) -> review AND reason names 'requests' with a
#               homoglyph/confusable justification.
#   (AFFIX)     'python-requests' (prefix, distance 7, Unknown own
#               downloads) -> review AND reason cites reputation-riding of
#               'requests'.
#   (GEN-AFFIX) 'data-numpy' (NON-allowlisted affix token — the 95%-evasion
#               class from the #3005 red-team) -> review AND reason cites
#               reputation-riding of 'numpy'.
#   (HOMO-AFFIX)'nｕmpy-x' (fullwidth homoglyph + arbitrary affix; evaded
#               raw-byte affix match, whole-name skeleton, AND mixed-script)
#               -> review AND reason cites reputation-riding of 'numpy'.
#   (LEGIT-FP)  'python-dateutil' (ON the popular seed list, itself a real
#               package) -> reason carries NO lexical-squat signal (no
#               typo-squat / homoglyph / mixed-script / reputation-riding) —
#               the false-positive guard, expected green on baseline AND fix.
#   (MIXED-FP)  'py中文tools' (multi-script, resembles nothing popular) ->
#               reason carries NO mixed-script/lexical-squat signal — the
#               proximity gate that stops the review-queue FP flood.
#
# Discriminating: GREEN on a #2956 image with the #3005 red-team fixes.
# RED on current main (pre-#2956): squat names exceed max_distance<=2, so
# their reasons are "popularity unknown" only — HOMOGLYPH/AFFIX/GEN-AFFIX/
# HOMO-AFFIX gates fail. Also RED on the first #2956 iteration (bounded affix
# allowlist + ungated mixed-script): GEN-AFFIX and HOMO-AFFIX produce no
# signal and MIXED-FP is spuriously flagged.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: admin login plus ~12 back-to-back API/DB calls.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
